   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "ONNX + DirectML",
   "start": 17.534,
   "duration": 16.906,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "4,400 in the demo",
   "start": 17.984,
   "duration": 16.456,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Four thousand four hundred people are playing this demo right now.\nTwo days after it went up. That's more than any demo I've taken apart.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 7.177
  },
  {
   "text": "It's a pixel-art Final Fantasy, and the build\nhas a machine learning runtime inside it.",
   "start": 7.427,
   "duration": 4.957
  },
  {
   "text": "FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE is the first HD-2D Final Fantasy.\nPixel characters, a 3D world, and the Octopath Traveler look.",
   "start": 16.234,
   "duration": 8.77
  },
  {
   "text": "Which makes sense, because it's the Octopath team. Team Asano at Square\nEnix, with a Tokyo studio called LANCARSE doing the co-development.",
   "start": 25.254,
   "duration": 9.136
  },
  {
   "text": "LANCARSE is the studio you've played without knowing it. Shin Megami\nTensei Strange Journey, Lost Dimension, The DioField Chronicle.",
   "start": 34.64,
   "duration": 8.483
  },
  {
   "text": "The story is season one of Brave Exvius, the mobile game, rebuilt. And in battle\nyou summon Visions, which are classic Final Fantasy characters. Cloud shows up.",
   "start": 43.373,
   "duration": 10.103
  },
  {
   "text": "The demo is not a slice. The Japanese title says it outright: the whole of\nchapter one, ahead of release. The full game lands October twenty second.",
   "start": 53.726,
   "duration": 9.789
  },
  {
   "text": "There are no reviews to read. Square Enix switches them off before launch. So\nthis one is the build and the people, which is the part I can actually check.",
   "start": 63.765,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "Steam publishes the file list for every demo. This\none is twenty six files, five point seven gigabytes.",
   "start": 71.845,
   "duration": 6.681
  },
  {
   "text": "It's Unreal Engine 5. You can tell from two file extensions,\nucas and utoc. That container format only exists in five.",
   "start": 78.776,
   "duration": 7.83
  },
  {
   "text": "Almost all of the size is content. One container is four point one\ngigabytes, the other one point one. That's five gigabytes for one chapter.",
   "start": 86.856,
   "duration": 8.3
  },
  {
   "text": "And the executable is four hundred and sixty seven megabytes. That's not a\nlauncher. That's the whole engine and the whole game, linked into one file.",
   "start": 95.406,
   "duration": 8.718
  },
  {
   "text": "Only fourteen DLLs ship, and every one of them is somebody else's. That's a very different\nshape from the Unity builds on this channel, where the package list is the story.",
   "start": 104.374,
   "duration": 10.103
  },
  {
   "text": "So with Unreal, the teardown is what's around the\nengine. And around this one there are a few surprises.",
   "start": 114.727,
   "duration": 6.054
  },
  {
   "text": "First. ONNX Runtime and DirectML. Together, thirty one megabytes. That's Unreal's\nneural network plugin. A machine learning inference runtime, in a pixel-art RPG.",
   "start": 121.031,
   "duration": 12.375
  },
  {
   "text": "What it's for, I can't see from a file list. It could be upscaling. It could be animation.\nIt could be a plugin dependency nobody trimmed. If you know, the comments are right there.",
   "start": 133.656,
   "duration": 10.651
  },
  {
   "text": "Second. NVIDIA Aftermath, for GPU crash reports, and MsQuic, which is\nthe transport under HTTP/3. So something in here phones home over QUIC.",
   "start": 144.557,
   "duration": 12.428
  },
  {
   "text": "Third, the audio. XAudio2 and Ogg Vorbis. No Wwise, no FMOD. A Final\nFantasy shipping on the engine's stock audio path is worth noting.",
   "start": 157.235,
   "duration": 10.39
  },
  {
   "text": "And then the slip. d3d12SDKLayers.dll. That's the DirectX 12 debug layer. Five\nand a half megabytes that exist to help a developer find bugs, shipped to players.",
   "start": 167.875,
   "duration": 12.898
  },
  {
   "text": "Next to it, a five megabyte debug fallback font, and a three byte staging config\nfile. None of it hurts you. All of it says the shipping config wasn't tightened.",
   "start": 181.023,
   "duration": 10.39
  },
  {
   "text": "Three episodes ago a three-person team shipped seven hundred megabytes of\ndebug symbols. Different scale, same mistake. It happens at Square Enix too.",
   "start": 191.663,
   "duration": 9.554
  },
  {
   "text": "One more date. The manifest says this build was made on July third. Two months\nbefore the demo went live. That's the buffer a publisher this size keeps.",
   "start": 201.467,
   "duration": 9.606
  },
  {
   "text": "Reception, then. There are no reviews,\nso here's the only number there is.",
   "start": 211.323,
   "duration": 4.434
  },
  {
   "text": "Four thousand four hundred people in the demo at once, on a Saturday, two days in.\nThe previous record on this channel was Guildrun at two thousand eight hundred.",
   "start": 216.007,
   "duration": 9.267
  },
  {
   "text": "A whole chapter for free, from the Octopath team, in a series\npeople already trust. The number isn't surprising. It's still big.",
   "start": 225.524,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 233.735,
   "duration": 2.109
  },
  {
   "text": "Unreal 5. Team Asano and LANCARSE. A four hundred and sixty seven\nmegabyte executable, an ML runtime, and the debug layer left in.",
   "start": 236.094,
   "duration": 9.92
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip. It's a full chapter, it's\nfree, and it goes away when the game ships.",
   "start": 246.264,
   "duration": 5.61
  },
  {
   "text": "If you build in Unreal, the thing to take from this is the shipping config. Open\nyour packaged folder and look for SDKLayers. If it's there, so is everyone else's.",
   "start": 252.124,
   "duration": 9.737
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read from the outside. If you worked on this and I got something wrong, say so\nand I'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 262.111,
   "duration": 10.233
  }
 ],
